From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:38:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 371/488] V2 runner: combine reads each request's scalars and
 drafts up front

The request's starts, lengths, last sampled token, draft row and confidence row
are read together, ahead of every store, and with dead rows each request takes a
block of its own, the forms round 3 of the TileLang completion experiment timed
fastest (level with Triton at decode, where production was +0.4 us). The kernel
key carries the drafts' width; every value written is unchanged.
